No rule qualifies as separately proved: `prove.sh` compiles `verification.k` with all five rules before every `kprove` invocation, and there is no earlier proof against a rule-free module with an exact matching statement. The three simplification rules are recursive equations for `derivAcc`, while the remaining two recursively define `noRefsVS`; all five therefore classify as `DEFINITION`.
